2025-10-07 19:33:44,667 [WARNING] Skipped idx=560: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='The context provided does not explicitly mention the number of TAp73 isoforms identified in humans. However, it does describe the expression of TAP73 and DeltaNP73 in malignant gliomas, indicating that the p73 gene encodes both transcriptionally active TAp73 and a dominant-negatively acting DeltaNp73. The text specifies that in humans, two TAp73 isoforms have been identified, which are differentially spliced. These include the full-length TAp73 and a shorter form that lacks the first 55 amino acids (TAp73-55). The presence of these isoforms has been studied in the context of their expression in various tissues, including normal brain and glial tumors, using semiquantitative RT-PCR. It is important to note that the expression of these isoforms can be affected by genetic alterations, such as the deletion of the common start site (CPS), which is associated with the loss of CDKN1C and an increase in TAp73 expression. However, it is distinct from the dominant-negative DeltaNp73 isoform, which is a separate product of the p73 gene and acts as a transcriptional repressor.'
